{
  "header": [
    "ECP-R9 — the connection path is pre-authorized in ANY connection state: a post-establishment",
    "connect-path EXECUTE carrying no author, capability or signature is not refused for their absence.",
    "",
    "Batch 2. Reached from `connectivity/keepalive_ping_pong`, which cites EXTENSION-NETWORK (not in this",
    "snapshot) — but its core half is §4.2, which IS. See FINDINGS F10."
  ],
  "id": "ECP-R9",
  "id_status": "allocated",
  "title": "After establishment, an EXECUTE to system/protocol/connect with no author, capability or signature is not refused on authentication or authorization grounds",
  "spec": "ENTITY-CORE-PROTOCOL §4.2 (first two bullets)",
  "spec_also": [
    "§3.2 ('All EXECUTE requests MUST include author and capability — except requests targeting the connection path')",
    "§4.7 (unknown connect operation -> 400 invalid_request; half-open ping -> 409)",
    "§5.2a (the 401/403 split for other paths)",
    "§9.1 (the floor row this id binds)"
  ],
  "snapshot": "entity-core-protocol/v0.8.2.21",
  "level": "MUST",
  "profile": [
    "core"
  ],
  "surface": "wire",
  "status": "draft",
  "routed": "docs/status/FINDINGS-FROM-AUTHORING.md F10",
  "reading": [
    "§4.2: \"`system/protocol/connect` is the sole pre-authorized path, IN ANY CONNECTION STATE — before and",
    "after establishment (0.8.2.6) ... a post-establishment `ping` bearing no `author`, no `capability`",
    "and no signature MUST be served, and a responder MUST NOT refuse it for their absence.\" And: \"EXECUTE",
    "targeting this path MUST be accepted without `author` or `capability` fields.\"",
    "",
    "ONE OBLIGATION, AND IT IS THE STATE QUALIFIER. Pre-establishment, the exemption is exercised by every",
    "hello there has ever been, and no peer fails it without failing everything. 0.8.2.6 added \"in any",
    "connection state\" because the POST-establishment half was being read the wrong way round (§5.1 as",
    "the rule, the connect path as an exception scoped to setup). So the discriminating probe is",
    "post-establishment, and that is this file.",
    "",
    "WHAT THIS FILE DELIBERATELY DOES NOT ASSERT — AND WHY IT IS A FINDING. §4.2 says a post-establishment",
    "`ping` \"MUST be served\". `ping` is defined nowhere in this snapshot: the word appears in §4.2, in",
    "§4.7's half-open paragraph (\"an unauthenticated `ping` on a half-open connection is 409\"), and nowhere",
    "else (`grep -n -w -i ping` over all three documents: §4.2 twice, §4.7 once; the §3.13 type comment",
    "says \"keepalive\", not `ping` — corrected 2026-09-12, review). Its definition is EXTENSION-NETWORK's. Two readings:",
    "  (A) the MUST is about the pre-authorization exemption; `ping` is the motivating example, and a",
    "      core-only peer that does not implement it answers §4.7's \"unknown connect operation\" row,",
    "      `400 invalid_request`, which is not a refusal \"for their absence\";",
    "  (B) core requires `ping` to be implemented, so `200` is the only conformant answer.",
    "§4.7's half-open paragraph leans B (\"a connect operation the responder implements\"); §4.7's own",
    "unknown-operation row, which exists for exactly this case, leans A. The reference oracle's owner",
    "records reading A in its own status log (\"`ping` required in the connect manifest at FULL profile",
    "(core profile unchanged)\"). We do not pick. So this file asserts only what BOTH readings require —",
    "the answer is not an authentication or authorization refusal and not a close — and records the",
    "status and code as a witness. Routed as F10.",
    "",
    "⚠ THE STATE QUALIFIER IS CONTRADICTED BY TWO OTHER PASSAGES, AND UNTIL RULED THIS FILE DOES NOT SCORE",
    "401. Found by review 2026-09-12; routed as F10's second question. Three passages, three scopes:",
    "  * §4.2: \"the sole pre-authorized path, in any connection state — before and after establishment\".",
    "  * §6.5's dispatch chain: \"URI = system/protocol/connect AND connection not established? -> Connection",
    "    handler (no auth required)\"; \"Otherwise: ... Verify request integrity (§5.2 verify_request ...)\".",
    "    A post-establishment connect-path EXECUTE takes the \"Otherwise\" branch, and an unauthenticated one",
    "    is refused auth-class — 401. §6.5 then says \"Connection pre-authorization is the sole dispatch",
    "    special case\", without a state.",
    "  * §4.7's half-open paragraph: \"the pre-authorized-connect exception (§3.3 line 773 / §5.1) is scoped",
    "    to an **established** connection, which a half-open one is not\" — the opposite scope to §6.5.",
    "§4.2 is the most specific and states that it corrects the older reading, and we lean to it. But a",
    "peer implementing §6.5's diagram literally answers 401, and that is a specification gap before it is",
    "an implementation bug. So 401/403 are a WITNESS here, not a refusal, until arch rules; a close stays a",
    "refusal, because no passage produces one.",
    "",
    "THE CONTROL IS WHAT MAKES THIS MEAN SOMETHING. A peer that never enforces authentication anywhere",
    "passes the conformant arm trivially. The control sends the same unauthenticated shape to a",
    "non-connect path and requires the auth-class refusal §4.2's third bullet and §5.2a require, proving the",
    "exemption is path-specific."
  ],
  "preconditions": {
    "grants": [],
    "identities": [
      "caller"
    ],
    "handlers": [],
    "posture_axes": [
      "seed_policy"
    ]
  },
  "arm": [
    {
      "name": "post-establishment-unauthenticated-connect",
      "kind": "conformant",
      "given": "an ESTABLISHED connection (§4.1 legs 1–2 complete); an EXECUTE to `system/protocol/connect`, operation `ping`, with no `author`, no `capability`, and no signature in `included`",
      "why": "§4.2's state qualifier.",
      "step": [
        {
          "op": "connect"
        },
        {
          "op": "send_execute_unauthenticated",
          "capture": "ping",
          "uri": "system/protocol/connect",
          "operation": "ping"
        }
      ],
      "witness": [
        {
          "field": "auth_class_refusal",
          "status": [
            401,
            403
          ],
          "why": "refused for the absence of author/capability/signature. §4.2 calls this the pre-0.8.2.6 misreading; §6.5's dispatch chain produces it (the 'connection not established' branch). PENDING F10's second question — moves to refuse if arch rules §4.2 governs. Recorded, not scored, until then."
        },
        {
          "field": "status_and_code",
          "why": "which reading the cohort implements. Recorded, never scored beyond the arms above."
        }
      ],
      "refuse": [
        {
          "outcome": "close",
          "why": "a close is a refusal too, and §4.2's 'MUST be served' excludes it under either reading."
        }
      ],
      "accept": [
        {
          "outcome": "coded_response",
          "status_not_in": [
            401,
            403
          ],
          "why": "§4.2's obligation is that the EXECUTE is not refused FOR THE ABSENCE of author, capability or signature. Any coded answer that is not auth-class is outside that refusal: 200 (reading B), 400 invalid_request (reading A, §4.7's unknown-connect-operation row), and a peer that implements `ping` and refuses OUR params shape. Which of those a peer gives is the status_and_code witness below, never scored here.\nAMENDED 2026-09-13, AFTER THE FIRST EXECUTION (F40). This arm listed exactly {200, 400 invalid_request}. Run against entity-core-go's entity-peer it FAILED on `400 invalid_params` — message \"ping params must be system/network/ping, got primitive/any\": the peer implements ping with EXTENSION-NETWORK's params type, which is not in this snapshot (F10), and refused our §3.2 empty-params shape. That is a served, non-auth answer. The enumerated accept set was narrower than this file's own title and reading; the defect was the requirement's, and only running it showed it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "control",
      "kind": "negative-control",
      "given": "the same established connection; the SAME unauthenticated shape sent to `system/tree`, operation `get`",
      "why": "MANDATORY ANTI-VACUITY. Proves the conformant arm's not-401 is the PATH EXEMPTION and not a peer that authenticates nothing. §4.2's third bullet: 'EXECUTE targeting any other path without valid authentication MUST be rejected per §5.2a: a missing/unverifiable author or signature is auth-class 401'.",
      "step": [
        {
          "op": "send_execute_unauthenticated",
          "capture": "tree",
          "uri": "system/tree",
          "operation": "get"
        }
      ],
      "assert": [
        {
          "kind": "status",
          "capture": "tree",
          "equals": 401
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "non-conformant-witness",
      "kind": "non-conformant",
      "given": "a peer that applies §5.1's author/capability requirement to every EXECUTE once the connection is established",
      "expect": "the post-establishment unauthenticated ping is refused 401",
      "why": "the exact misreading 0.8.2.6 was written to correct: the general rule and its exception, the wrong way round."
    }
  ],
  "notes": {
    "peer_attributable": true,
    "oracle_check": "connectivity/keepalive_ping_pong",
    "oracle_note": "provenance, and PARTIAL: that check cites EXTENSION-NETWORK §5.1/§12.1, whose ping semantics (pong shape, keepalive loop) are not in this snapshot and are not authored. This file is the core half only. F10."
  }
}
